                    {
                        "sense_id": "1f9288a0-155a-3d44-87e4-42bf1769b608",
                        "entry_id": "48d61834-913e-37b7-af9e-a1d0e4fd4828",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Deserving of being hanged."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "270ed07b-e57f-4c17-946c-88075e0806fe",
                                "sense_id": "1f9288a0-155a-3d44-87e4-42bf1769b608",
                                "text": "Sometymes our coyne, could stop a gappe, / And purchace pardon by a traine: / But gallows lucke, and ropripe happe, / At length was gwerdon for our paine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "672f1ea2-1fa3-4110-94e1-88853f192ec4",
                                "sense_id": "1f9288a0-155a-3d44-87e4-42bf1769b608",
                                "text": "As we argued already, Shakespeare's representation of the rope-ripe shrew likely was inspired by abundant accounts of the well-hanged and well-hung shrewmouse."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e80b3e44-2001-30e1-b2a1-ae72543e1f2d",
                        "entry_id": "48d61834-913e-37b7-af9e-a1d0e4fd4828",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Punishable by being hanged."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "19b780a2-a626-4a2a-8c36-e5de1e2e5a96",
                                "sense_id": "e80b3e44-2001-30e1-b2a1-ae72543e1f2d",
                                "text": "Therefore the reporting of our tale, may ſone appere plain if we firſt expreſſe our minde in plaine words, and not ſeeke theſe roperipe termes, which betraie rather a foole, then commende a wiſe man[…]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "443babc9-6d0b-4029-8f4f-547ea6f096e8",
                                "sense_id": "e80b3e44-2001-30e1-b2a1-ae72543e1f2d",
                                "text": "Lord, how you roule in your rope-ripe termes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
